  "arm_notes": {
    "periodic_residual_counts": "EXP-P32/P34/P35 arm unchanged (frozen PLR-lite embedding + residual backbone, blocks Dropout .1, counts workload), old code path; keeps its embed_residual flag, so the robust-clip family predicate is tested first in the runner and scorer",
    "pitcher_id_periodic_residual_counts": "Reference entry + pitcher_id block (direct_pitcher_id_model): TRAIN-only vocabulary of pitcher ids with >= 100 TRAIN rows (sorted), UNK 0 otherwise (rare TRAIN pitchers and ids first seen after TRAIN), index appended as the last context column and stripped before the frozen maps; z += P @ T[idx] (T zeros [n_vocab + 1, 8], P [128, 8] private generator seed + 7919) so the untrained network equals the reference at the same seed (P38 entry verbatim) Pitcher-only cell of the 2x2, paired with the other arms at the same seeds (P40 / P42 seeds are never paired with these).",
    "batter_id_periodic_residual_counts": "P38 id path on the batter column: TRAIN-only vocabulary (batters with >= 100 TRAIN rows, sorted ids, UNK 0), zero-init table [n_vocab + 1, 8], projection 128 x 8 from the private generator seed + 7919 + 1009, z += P T[idx]. Batter ids come from the pinned sidecar.",
    "batter_id_row_shuffle_periodic_residual_counts": "Batter-id network, parameters and compute; before the vocabulary lookup the split's `batter` column is permuted across rows by np.random.default_rng([43001, split position]) (fixed, independent of labels, features and the model seed). Index frequencies / UNK share kept, row -> batter association destroyed (information-free).",
    "pitcher_batter_id_periodic_residual_counts": "Two id paths, additive: the P38 pitcher path verbatim (projection seed + 7919) and the batter path above (seed + 7919 + 1009). Index columns (pitcher, batter).",
    "epoch_cap": "Epoch cap 60, patience 5 for both arms (as EXP-P34-P37). fit.json records cap, epochs_run, best_epoch and stopped_by per fit",
    "parameters": "Reference 244898; each id path adds (n_vocab + 1) x 8 + 128 x 8 (n_vocab per column measured from TRAIN, recorded per fit, re-derived and checked by the scorer)",
    "capacity": "Batter id vs row-shuffle is parameter- and compute-matched with information removed; the control matches the id path, not a generic wider backbone. Pitcher + batter vs pitcher adds the batter path; pitcher + batter vs batter adds the pitcher path (neither matched; P40 holds the pitcher controls)."
  },
